In the water’s rest frame the light travels at \(u = \dfrac{c}{n} = \dfrac{c}{4/3} = \dfrac{3c}{4}\).

The tube moves relative to the lab at \(v_{\text{tube}} = \frac{1}{2}c\).

Use the relativistic velocity addition formula:
\[
v_{\text{lab}} = \frac{u + v_{\text{tube}}}{1 + \frac{uv_{\text{tube}}}{c^{2}}}
= \frac{\frac{3c}{4} + \frac{c}{2}}{1 + \frac{\frac{3c}{4}\,\frac{c}{2}}{c^{2}}}
= \frac{\frac{5c}{4}}{1 + \frac{3}{8}}
= \frac{\frac{5c}{4}}{\frac{11}{8}}
= \frac{5}{4}\cdot\frac{8}{11}c
= \frac{10}{11}c .
\]

Thus the speed of the light in the water relative to the lab is \(10/11\,c\).

