For a simple Lorentzian line the full width at half maximum (FWHM) Δν (in Hz) is related to the transverse relaxation time T₂ by  

\[
\Delta\nu = \frac{1}{\pi\,T_2}
\]

Given  

- \(T_2 = 15 \text{ ms} = 0.015 \text{ s}\)

\[
\Delta\nu = \frac{1}{\pi \times 0.015}
          = \frac{1}{0.0471238898}
          \approx 21.2 \text{ Hz}
\]

So the linewidth is approximately **21.2 Hz**.

